.TH BAO 1 "2026-09-06" "NuCode" "LAN vault"
.SH NAME
bao \- OpenBao vault as deployed on the NuCode LAN
.SH DESCRIPTION
.TP
.BI bao
The OpenBao command-line client (a static Go binary, version 2.6.2 on this box). This page documents OpenBao AS DEPLOYED on the NuCode LAN, not the full upstream CLI (for that run: bao -h , or see the OpenBao docs).
.PP
The vault runs as a Docker container named bao from /data/NuCode/Bao, reachable at https://192.168.88.18:8200 on the LAN and loopback only, behind a self-signed certificate.
.PP
Day to day you drive it through bao-kit(1), which sets the address, the CA cert and the token for you; reach for raw bao only for things bao-kit does not wrap.
.SH DEPLOYMENT

.PP
The vault is a docker compose service named bao, defined in .BR /data/NuCode/Bao/docker-compose.yml, using image .BR openbao/openbao:2.6.2.

.PP
Raft storage lives on a named docker volume, so recreating the container does not lose data.

.PP
The listener binds 0.0.0.0:8200 inside the container; the host publishes it on 127.0.0.1:8200 and 192.168.88.18:8200.

.PP
TLS is a self-signed cert; clients must trust .BR tls/bao.crt (BAO_CACERT).

.PP
The audit device and the kv v2 engine at kv/ are enabled at init time.
.SH ENVIRONMENT

.TP
.BI BAO_ADDR
The address of the server: https://192.168.88.18:8200.
.TP
.BI BAO_CACERT
Path to tls/bao.crt, so the client trusts the self-signed cert.
.TP
.BI BAO_TOKEN
The auth token; if unset, bao-kit loads the cached login from ~/.config/openbao/token.
.TP
.BI eval "$(bao-kit env)"
The quickest way to set all three.
.SH DAILY USE

.PP
The host sleeps at night and the vault SEALS on every boot, so the day starts sealed. The morning ritual is:

.nf
bao-kit unseal
.fi
(reads the stored key, unseals)

.nf
bao-kit login
.fi
(caches a 12h operator token)

.PP
After that, bao-kit status should show sealed: False and a valid token. Raw equivalents exist (bao operator unseal, bao login) but the kit is the path.
.SH COMMANDS YOU USE

.TP
.BI bao status
Seal and HA status.
.TP
.BI bao operator unseal KEY
Submit an unseal key share (bao-kit unseal wraps this).
.TP
.BI bao kv get \-mount=kv PATH
Read a secret (prints it; mind the transcript).
.TP
.BI bao kv put \-mount=kv PATH field=value
Replace a secret (whole secret).
.TP
.BI bao kv patch \-mount=kv PATH field=value
Merge fields into a secret (this is what bao-kit put uses).
.TP
.BI bao token lookup
.TP
.BI bao token create
Inspect or mint tokens.
.TP
.BI bao login \-method=userpass username=ziggy
Authenticate.
.TP
.BI bao unwrap TOKEN
Unwrap a response-wrapping token.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
.BI Connection refused on 8200 though docker ps shows the container Up
Docker started the container without installing the host port publish (docker inspect shows PortBindings set but NetworkSettings.Ports empty; nothing listens on host :8200). It follows iptables churn from the LAN NAT link.
.FI cd /data/NuCode/Bao && docker compose down && docker compose up -d
The raft data is on the named volume, so nothing is lost. Verify with docker port bao (expect both 127.0.0.1:8200 and 192.168.88.18:8200).
.TP
.BI Every call 403s right after login
A stale exported BAO_TOKEN is shadowing the fresh cached token.
.FI unset BAO_TOKEN
before the command.
.TP
.BI sealed: True after a reboot
Expected; run bao-kit unseal.
.SH FILES

.TP
.BI /data/NuCode/Bao/docker-compose.yml
the compose service.
.TP
.BI /data/NuCode/Bao/tls/bao.crt
the self-signed CA cert (BAO_CACERT).
.TP
.BI /data/NuCode/Bao/config/
the OpenBao server config (declares the listener and the file audit device).
.TP
.BI ~/.config/openbao/init.json
unseal key and root token, mode 600.
.TP
.BI ~/.config/openbao/token
cached operator login, mode 600.
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
.BI bao-kit(1)
The wrapper you use day to day.
.TP
.BI /data/NuCode/Bao/README.md
The vault repo README is authoritative.
.TP
.BI bao -h
The full upstream CLI is in bao -h and the OpenBao documentation.
.TP
.BI man ./docs/bao.1
Read this page without installing it: man ./docs/bao.1
